From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ricktav <82380971+ricktav@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 16:43:10 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] block: asp: Start the ANS after RTKit owns the mailbox

The probe started the ANS CPU in apple_asp_setup_firmware(), before
devm_apple_rtkit_init() started the mailbox. iBoot leaves the A7's ANS
firmware initialised, and such a firmware sends HELLO within
milliseconds of the start bit. On an iPad mini 2 (J85) running a kernel
whose A7 mailbox enabled its FIFOs only when RTKit started it, that HELLO
was lost and the probe failed with "Failed to wake ASP" (-ETIME) on every
boot.

The A7 mailbox now enables its FIFOs when it probes, but the order
should not depend on the mailbox variant: the A8 and A8X mailboxes still
enable theirs only in apple_mbox_start(). Program the firmware window as
before, and start the CPU after RTKit has started the mailbox, right
before waking it.

Also stop the CPU at AKF_V1_CPU_CONTROL on the error and remove paths.
They wrote 0 to AKF_V1_CPU_CONTROL_START, a bit value used as an offset
(0x10, the low half of the IOP remap address), so the CPU kept running.

Assisted-by: LLM
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: ricktav <82380971+ricktav@users.noreply.github.com>
Link: https://github.com/OrchardLinux/orchard/pull/221#issuecomment-7124272492
---
 drivers/block/asp.c | 16 ++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/block/asp.c b/drivers/block/asp.c
index 1939347f3..2b538e681 100644
--- a/drivers/block/asp.c
+++ b/drivers/block/asp.c
@@ -1095,10 +1095,6 @@ static int apple_asp_setup_firmware(struct apple_asp *asp)
 	writel(AKF_V1_LITTLE_ENDIAN,
 	       asp->akf_base + AKF_V1_ENDIANNESS);
 
-	/* start ASP */
-	writel(AKF_V1_CPU_CONTROL_START,
-	       asp->akf_base + AKF_V1_CPU_CONTROL);
-
 	return 0;
 }
 
@@ -1300,6 +1296,14 @@ static int apple_asp_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 
 	init_completion(&asp->init_done);
 
+	/*
+	 * Start the ANS only once RTKit owns the mailbox. iBoot leaves the A7's
+	 * ANS firmware initialised, and then it sends HELLO within milliseconds
+	 * of the start bit: before RTKit has started the mailbox, that message
+	 * can be lost and the wake below times out.
+	 */
+	writel(AKF_V1_CPU_CONTROL_START, asp->akf_base + AKF_V1_CPU_CONTROL);
+
 	ret = apple_rtkit_wake(asp->rtk);
 	if (ret) {
 		ret = dev_err_probe(dev, ret, "Failed to wake ASP");
@@ -1336,7 +1340,7 @@ static int apple_asp_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 out_rtkit:
 	apple_rtkit_shutdown(asp->rtk);
 out_stop_iop:
-	writel(0, asp->akf_base + AKF_V1_CPU_CONTROL_START);
+	writel(0, asp->akf_base + AKF_V1_CPU_CONTROL);
 
 	return ret;
 }
@@ -1364,7 +1368,7 @@ static void apple_asp_remove(struct platform_device *pdev)
 
 	dma_free_coherent(asp->dev, ASP_QUEUE_SIZE, asp->q, asp->q_iova);
 
-	writel(0, asp->akf_base + AKF_V1_CPU_CONTROL_START);
+	writel(0, asp->akf_base + AKF_V1_CPU_CONTROL);
 }
 
 
